WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:09.821
The princess jumped into the lake.

2
00:00:09.822 --> 00:00:14.090
Underwater, she grabbed the prince's shoulders and tugged.

3
00:00:14.091 --> 00:00:17.344
But she couldn't move him.

4
00:00:17.345 --> 00:00:21.355
She came up for air and almost screamed.

5
00:00:21.356 --> 00:00:25.653
The water was up to the prince's eyes!

6
00:00:25.654 --> 00:00:27.783
Ellen tilted his head back.

7
00:00:27.784 --> 00:00:32.394
His nose and mouth were above the surface now.

8
00:00:32.395 --> 00:00:36.473
"But he's not breathing!" she thought in a panic.

9
00:00:36.474 --> 00:00:39.626
"What should I do?"

10
00:00:39.627 --> 00:00:45.133
Suddenly love—and water—brought back all her strength.

11
00:00:45.134 --> 00:00:49.883
She dived in again and pulled with her whole might.

12
00:00:49.884 --> 00:00:53.934
Finally, an arm came out of the hole.

13
00:00:53.935 --> 00:00:57.351
The rest of his body quickly followed.

14
00:00:57.352 --> 00:01:02.266
Reader, no one knows how the princess got him into the boat.

15
00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:04.490
But somehow she did this.

16
00:01:04.491 --> 00:01:11.817
Then she rowed the boat to shore as fast as she could.

17
00:01:11.818 --> 00:01:17.914
Using all her strength again, she pulled the prince onto land.

18
00:01:17.915 --> 00:01:23.207
His cheeks were pale, and his eyes were closed.

19
00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:28.495
"I'm too late," she thought. "He's dead!"

20
00:01:28.496 --> 00:01:30.918
Ellen's chest felt tight.

21
00:01:30.919 --> 00:01:40.395
She let out a strange sound, and her eyes filled with . . . tears!

22
00:01:40.396 --> 00:01:45.257
As she cried for the first time ever, raindrops began to fall.

23
00:01:45.258 --> 00:01:47.380
And it wasn't an ordinary rain.

24
00:01:47.381 --> 00:01:52.301
It was the colors of rubies, sapphires, and emeralds.

25
00:01:52.302 --> 00:01:55.167
The rain grew stronger.

26
00:01:55.168 --> 00:01:59.436
Soon water flowed down mountains like liquid gold.

27
00:01:59.437 --> 00:02:02.852
Brooks and rivers streamed again.

28
00:02:02.853 --> 00:02:07.021
Babies' eyes filled with tiny tears.

29
00:02:07.022 --> 00:02:11.826
The water in the lake rose higher and higher.

30
00:02:11.827 --> 00:02:16.762
So did the water in Agnes' cellars.

31
00:02:16.763 --> 00:02:25.501
Crash! A powerful river suddenly burst through the cellars' doors and passages.

32
00:02:25.502 --> 00:02:29.354
"Oh no!" Agnes screamed.

33
00:02:29.355 --> 00:02:36.024
The churning flood water swept her away.

34
00:02:36.025 --> 00:02:40.654
The princess continued to cry.

35
00:02:40.655 --> 00:02:48.383
She cried so hard, she didn't see the prince open his eyes.

36
00:02:48.384 --> 00:02:56.858
"Are you crying for me?" he asked.

37
00:02:56.859 --> 00:03:04.137
"You're alive!" The princess leaped up, forgetting to grab rocks.

38
00:03:04.138 --> 00:03:08.960
But she didn't float away.

39
00:03:08.961 --> 00:03:13.647
Instead she tumbled back down onto the ground!

40
00:03:13.648 --> 00:03:17.097
"You fell!" The prince was amazed.

41
00:03:17.098 --> 00:03:29.986
"That means . . . You have gravity!"

42
00:03:29.987 --> 00:03:38.379
Everyone in the kingdom rejoiced.

43
00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:46.343
Soon afterward Ellen and the prince got married.

44
00:03:46.344 --> 00:03:50.479
They had many children, who all had gravity.

45
00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:58.910
Together they laughed and cried, and lived happily ever after.

